.TH CORE-TERMINAL 1 "September 2026" "Core Terminal 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
core-terminal \- GTK4 terminal emulator using VTE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B core-terminal
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B core-terminal
opens a GTK4 terminal window and starts the configured login shell. Each tab
uses a VTE terminal widget and a separate child process group.
.PP
The Settings window contains General, Profiles, Window Groups, and Encodings
pages. Profile pages cover Text, Window, Tab, Shell, Keyboard, and Advanced
settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/core-terminal/default-profiles.json
Project-owned profiles installed by the Debian package.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/core-terminal/settings.json
User settings. If XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset, Core Terminal uses
.IR $HOME/.config/core-terminal/settings.json .
On Unix, the file is written with mode 0600.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute directory used for the user settings file.
.TP
.B HOME
Fallback parent directory for user settings when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
.TP
.B SHELL
Login shell used when no absolute shell override is saved.
.SH LIMITATIONS
GTK4 and the Wayland compositor control top-level placement. Core Terminal
doesn't restore macOS-style screen coordinates, live process state, Dock tile
contents, or Secure Keyboard Entry. VTE controls terminal protocol modes and
the runtime encoding remains UTF-8.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The process returns a non-zero status when GTK application startup fails.
